abstract: >-
  The Conciseness Framework constructs a deductively closed, zero-forward-reference
  scientific and philosophical unification spanning foundational epistemology and
  modal ontology (Pillar 1: The Foundation of Knowledge Theory, v2.10), domain
  epistemology and ontological curvature (Pillar 2: The Finite Infinity Framework,
  v2.0), universal dynamical selection calculus (Pillar 3: The Actualization Theory,
  v6.0), computational complexity and unsimulable reality (Pillar 4: The Computational
  Knowledge Theory, v4.0), and embodied cognition and knowledge-density acceleration
  (Pillar 5: Consciousness Operations as Prime Reductions, v4.0). Each pillar is
  accompanied by standalone mathematical verification scripts and publication-grade
  figures validating all analytical claims and numerical simulations.
